      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When transporting your bike to a new location within Indranagar or abroad, it is essential to provide accurate and comprehensive documentation. Below, we detail the vital paperwork required for a smooth and secure bike transportation process:</p>

	<p>The Registration Certificate (RC) is an important document that proves your ownership of the bike. To ensure the safety and legality of your transportation, it is crucial to provide a self-attested photocopy of your RC.</p>

	<p>Proof of Vehicle Usage (PUC) is a certificate issued annually that confirms the bike meets emission standards. A valid PUC is essential for transportation to demonstrate your bike's current status. Ensure that your PUC is up-to-date before proceeding with the transportation.</p>

	<p>Insurance plays a crucial role in protecting both you and the transportation company. Provide a valid insurance certificate, ensuring that your bike is covered during the transportation process. Make sure the certificate covers both your bike and the transportation company.</p>

	<p>An International Bike Association (IBA) approved consignment bill of lading is an official document that outlines the details of the shipment, such as the sender, receiver, bike specifications, and agreed-upon terms and conditions. This document serves as a binding agreement between you and the transportation company.</p>

	<p>To ensure maximum protection for your bike during transportation, it is advisable to opt for a marine transit insurance that covers the full value of your bike. This comprehensive insurance policy ensures that in case of any damages or losses during transit, you are fully reimbursed for the declared value of your bike.</p>
<p>It is essential to obtain a 100% declared-value insurance policy to safeguard your investment.</p>
